{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"a3182fef-eaa3-4280-97fa-6356a420cc0a","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have audited the MCP server against the standard checks that real MCP clients trip over (following the inspection protocol documented in [`notes/check-your-mcp-server-in-a-few-minutes.md`](file:///tmp/h-X41XUt/notes/check-your-mcp-server-in-a-few-minutes.md)) and recorded the full findings in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-X41XUt/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary of Findings\n\n- **Overall status:** **has the problem**\n- **Passing checks:**\n  - **C1 (Tool list without token):** `initialize`, `tools/list`, and `server/discover` answer unauthenticated callers cleanly.\n  - **C3 (Session survival):** Valid calls succeed immediately after errors within the same `Mcp-Session-Id`.\n  - **C4 (Published outputSchema honoured):** Read-only tools return conforming `structuredContent`.\n  - **C5 (Serialization):** Responses serialize cleanly without leaking non-JSON types.\n  - **C7 (Logging):** Structured per-call logs are emitted to `sys.stderr`.\n  - **C8 (Tool count and names):** 3 tools present, all names adhere to `^[a-zA-Z0-9_-]{1,64}$`.\n  - **C9 (Version negotiation):** Honestly responds with implemented version `2025-06-18` instead of echoing unknown version strings like `\"banana\"`.\n\n- **Failing checks:**\n  - **C2 (Tool refusals sent as protocol errors):** Calling a read-only tool with a missing parameter or non-existent ID throws JSON-RPC `-32602` error responses instead of HTTP 200 tool results with `isError: true`. Client SDKs raise exceptions on JSON-RPC errors, preventing LLMs from inspecting the error message and recovering.\n  - **C6 (Surface drift \u0026 lock):** No surface lock file is committed to prevent surface drift, and `server.py` advertises `resources` capability at `initialize` while returning HTTP 401 on `resources/list`.\n  - **C10 (Weak output schema):** `search_notes` declares a bare `outputSchema: {\"type\": \"object\"}` with no required fields or constraints, allowing corrupted outputs to pass validation.\n\nThe server files in the repository were left untouched.\n","duration_seconds":124.61402,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":108241,"output_tokens":4804,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":456566,"total_tokens":113045}}}
